            <profile id="e37e-bda7-3035-a9dc" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon. May have shield (+2 pts), light armour (+3 pts), longbow (+3 pts), javelins (+2 pts). May be mounted on a horse (free, Movement 8"), or in a light chariot, heavy chariot or on an elephant (bought at additional points cost from the list). A general on a horse may have a thrusting spear (+2 pts) and horse barding (+4 pts). The army must have a General. (Armies of Antiquity p.19)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="dc47-eb8f-fa34-c76b" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
