  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="7046-e42f-fcb4-3c7e" name="Ancient Indian (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ANCIENT INDIAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.18-19), 500 BC - 500 AD (Mauryan, Gupta, Kushan and Bactrian Greek kingdoms).
Characters: the army must have a General and may have an Army Standard Bearer. Elephants, Chariots &amp; Cavalry up to half the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter, with at most one elephant per 500 points (the elephant limit is applied to the Elephants unit).
Allies: Indian armies may have allies drawn from the Cataphract (Scythian mercenaries) and Ancient Greek (Bactrian Greek allies) lists (not built here: make a separate small roster).
Used To Elephants: Indian infantry do not fear elephants; Indian cavalry and chariots only fear them. Indian Longbow: treated as a longbow; downgrade all longbows to bows at -1 pt per model if you prefer.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Elephants, Chariots &amp; Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
